# Line-ending policy for seoboost-skill-set.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
# The repo is worked from macOS, Linux and — since 2026-08-04 — Windows. Without
# a .gitattributes the stored line endings depend entirely on each machine's
# `core.autocrlf`. Git for Windows defaults it to `true` (safe), but a contributor
# who sets it to `false` would commit real CRLF, and the 13 shell scripts here
# would then fail on every POSIX host with `$'\r': command not found`.
# This file removes that dependency: the repo decides, not the machine.
#
# EFFECT ON EXISTING HISTORY: NONE.
# Audited before adding, with `git ls-files --eol` over all 1038 tracked files:
#   989 blobs  i/lf     (already LF)
#    35 blobs  i/-text  (binary, correctly detected: png/pdf/docx/pptx)
#    13 blobs  i/none   (empty, e.g. .gitkeep)
#     0 blobs  i/crlf or i/mixed  <-- nothing to renormalize
# So `text=auto` rewrites no file and produces no diff. Verified afterwards with
# `git add --renormalize .` staging nothing but this file.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Default: normalize every text file to LF *inside the repository*.
# Checkout remains governed by core.autocrlf, so a Windows working tree may still
# show CRLF locally — harmless, and it never reaches a commit.
* text=auto

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Files executed on POSIX hosts must be LF in the WORKING TREE too, not just in
# the repo — a Windows checkout of these gets copied to Linux/macOS servers as-is.
# A stray CR breaks bash outright and makes shellcheck report SC1017 on every line.
*.sh        text eol=lf
*.service   text eol=lf
*.plist     text eol=lf

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Binaries — never transform. Git already auto-detects the four types currently
# tracked; these are declared so a future addition (a .zip export, a font, an
# .xlsx deliverable) can never be mangled by the text=auto heuristic.
*.png       binary
*.jpg       binary
*.jpeg      binary
*.gif       binary
*.webp      binary
*.ico       binary
*.svgz      binary
*.pdf       binary
*.docx      binary
*.xlsx      binary
*.pptx      binary
*.zip       binary
*.gz        binary
*.tar       binary
*.woff      binary
*.woff2     binary
*.ttf       binary
*.otf       binary
